_out\\\"`, `lastStatus`) becomes `outcome: \\\"pending\\\"` with `status` holding the run's last status.\\n- **`delivery.openPullRequest({ branch, files, message, title?, body?, base?, draft? })`**: `git switch -c` (skipped if the branch is already checked out), then `delivery.commit({ push: true })`, then `gh.prCreate`. If the branch already has an open PR, it returns that one with `created: false`. Branch names are validated before any Git call.\\n- **`pr.merge({ number, method, repo?, deleteBranch?, sync? })`**: refuses a PR that isn't open, merges, and with `sync: true` switches to the PR's base branch and runs `git pull --ff-only`. A failed sync comes back as `synced: { ok: false, error }`, not an exception, because the merge has already happened.\\n- The pit-delivery skill (with type-checked `pit-example` blocks), `.pi/functions/README.md`, and CHANGELOG are updated.\\n\\n## Validation\\n- `delivery.validate({ coverage: true, packageCheck: true })`: all gates pass.\\n- Existing wait tests updated to the pending contract. New tests cover `ci.waitForCommit` lifting a pending outcome and hint, `openPullRequest` ordering, branch/PR reuse, and input rejection, and `pr.merge` sync ordering, no-sync, a failed sync, and a non-open PR.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- [ ] After #385 merges and Pi reloads: confirm `functions.getSaved(\\\"delivery.openPullRequest\\\")` and `functions.getSaved(\\\"pr.merge\\\")` load, and that a short `pr.waitForChecks({ timeoutMs: 1000 })` returns `outcome: \\\"pending\\\"` with a hint.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/386\"}\n","code":0},{"id":2,"traceSequence":3,"command":"gh \"api\" \"repos/cv/pit/pulls/386\" \"--method\" \"PATCH\" \"-f\" \"body=Part of #383 (workflow composites and waits). It uses `git.switchBranch`, `git.pull`, and `git.revParse` from #385, which has merged; this branch is rebased onto `main`.\\n\\n## Changes\\n- **Waits return pending on timeout**: `ci.waitForRun`, `ci.waitForCommit`, and `pr.waitForChecks` return 